    "description": "Magellan 9300i or Magellan 9400i scanner/scale (models 939404 and 939406), Class III, mains operated, self-indicating, weight only, single or dual interval, Non-Automatic Weighing Instrument designed for direct sales to the public. Diecast base unit supports the load cell, barcode scanner assembly, main board and analogue boards; steel L-shaped load receptor mounted on four supporting points of the scale sub-assembly. Designed to be flush-mounted in a fixed position in a checkout surface; may be fitted with a level indicator. Devices: initial zero setting device, semi-automatic zero setting device, zero tracking device, automatic zero setting device, zero indicator, gravity compensation. Interfaces: POS terminal (RJ10), remote display (RJ4), scale host (RJ10), auxiliary port (RJ10), EAS port (RJ45), power (Molex 3 pin), USB, image port. Legally relevant parameters stored in EEPROM with software identification version numbers 1-70-28 and 2-0-0; calibration mode access only via a switch behind a sealing cap; tamper-evident securing of EEPROM, calibration switch and load cell."
